Tamiasciurus hudsonicus"], "owl>wolf": ["g", "Canis lupus", "Strix nebulosa"], "bear>wolf": ["g", "Canis lupus", "Ursus americanus"]}, "story": "Canada's boreal forest covers almost 60% of the country. Spruce, pine and aspen feed snowshoe hares, red squirrels and beavers, and spruce budworm eat spruce. Lynx hunt hares, and the two animals' numbers rise and fall together in a famous cycle.", "matters": "Fires and insect outbreaks regularly kill large stands, leaving even-aged forest and changing soil nutrients. That cycle of disturbance shapes the whole boreal."}